# .gitignore — public research repository
#
# Design rule: exclude RAW DATA, LARGE BLOBS, GENERATED CACHES and SECRETS — but NEVER exclude a
# tracked scientific artifact. A too-broad rule here would silently remove the ability to check a
# published number, which is a worse failure than a large repository.
#
# The exclusion set is deliberately NARROW and NAME-BASED rather than extension-based, so that a
# `.json`, `.csv` or `.npz` which is genuine evidence is never swallowed by accident.
#
# Verify the effect of any change with:
#     git status --porcelain --ignored | Select-String '^!!'
# and confirm nothing under */evidence/, */configs/, */outputs/ or docs/ is listed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw datasets — not redistributed, never committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/
**/raw/*.set
**/raw/*.fdt
**/raw/*.cnt
**/raw/*.mat
**/raw/*.edf
**/raw/*.bdf
**/raw/*.vhdr
**/raw/*.eeg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large waveform / feature arrays — regenerable via prepare_data.py
# (the published manifest and splits are .csv/.json and are NOT matched here)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/waveforms/
*.npy
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.parquet
*.feather

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model checkpoints — represented by CHECKPOINT_MANIFEST.csv instead of bytes.
# The single published exception is the 1.2 MB legacy prototype checkpoint.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
!archive/legacy/ns_sd_prototype_2026/feature_extracting/feature_data/lstm_fatigue_best.pt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Archives and bulk payloads
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.iso

# Discarded by exception: keep the third-party pin manifests, which are small JSON.
!shared/ds004902_source_trunk/third_party/*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python build / bytecode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs, scratch and runtime output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*~
*.norm

# External frozen phase caches (fold Grams, BCIT staging) live outside the repository by design.
# If one is ever staged in-tree, keep it out — but do NOT exclude the published outputs/ or
# evidence/ trees, which hold the manifests and statistics the READMEs cite.
**/folds/
**/integrity_test/
**/partial_run*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials — must never be committed
#
# NOTE on scope: these rules are ANCHORED to the repository root. An unanchored `*secret*` matches
# at every depth and silently excluded `docs/refresh/scan_secrets.py` -- the repository's own
# secret SCANNER -- from the tree. A security rule that removes your security tooling is a bug.
# Credential material belongs at the root and in config directories, not in a docs tool.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.env
/.env.*
!/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.ppk
*.pfx
*.p12
/id_rsa*
/id_ed25519*
/known_hosts
/.ssh/
/credentials*
/secrets*
/remote_state.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment / tooling
#
# NOTE on `.vscode/`: the rule is ANCHORED to the repository root (`/.vscode/`). An unanchored
# `.vscode/` matches at every depth and would silently drop
# archive/legacy/legacy_ns_sd_prototype/.vscode/settings.json -- which is part of the byte-exact
# historical record of what this repository used to publish. The editor's local settings are
# ignored; the archived copy is preserved.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.conda/
.idea/
/.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb
